es (areas, people, dimensions, documents, unplaced), each one expand away; (4) FOCUS — material loaded for your focus, LAST. The map, coverage, and doors never vary with your focus.\n\n^-marked entries are compressed stubs carrying child addresses. Their narration and any surfaced witness quotes are verbatim-accurate — quote them as-is — but a stub carries no provenance (source, date, supersession). Expand (aswritten_expand with the IRIs you need) before any claim that turns on WHEN or by WHOM something was said, or whether it is still the current framing. Witness-depth sections below already carry full provenance.\n\nThis entry is BOUNDED — the whole graph is deliberately not inlined. Every node is reachable within a bounded number of expands: before concluding the perspective is silent on your subject, check the map and coverage, then expand the door whose axis would hold it (^Thematic for topics and areas, ^People for anyone, ^Documents for a call or memory, ^Unplaced for loose positions). Absence becomes signal only after the relevant door shows nothing.\n\n# The map — this graph's richest ground (top fidelity band)\n\n\n# Coverage — narrated, from four directions\n\n\n# Doors — pick an axis\n\n[ ^Thematic — every area (0) by name ] [ ^People 1 ] [ ^Dimensions — 0 axes ] [ ^Documents 0 ] [ ^Unplaced 0 ]\nEach door expands to a complete axis: aswritten_expand(iris=[\"Thematic\"]) — same coords as this perspective. Nothing in the graph is outside every door.\n\n# Focus: Quantum Widget Decision, PostgreSQL to QuantumDB migration, removal of knowledge, forgetting decisions (witness depth — per-call section)\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\n### ns__Strategy\n\nchildren (witness depth):\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst\ntype: ns__Decision\nXena: 'Every engagement starts with a diagnostic phase. Never propose solutions before understanding the system.' Two weeks, $5K, 8+ stakeholder interviews.\nDiagnostic First Methodology\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping\ntype: ns__Decision\nVisualize where decisions happen and where knowledge lives. Deliverable: knowledge gap report with prioritized recommendations.\nKnowledge Gap Mapping\nunder: ns__Strategy\n\n### ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst  (already in your context)\n\n### ns__Actor_XenaGithubber\ntype: ns__Actor\nIndependent consultant specializing in knowledge mapping and organizational diagnostics.\nXena Githubber\n\n\nserved: ^ns__Actor_XenaGithubber, ^ns__Decision_DiagnosticFirst, ^ns__Decision_KnowledgeMapping, ^ns__Strategy\n(pass this list back as `have` on your next expand — content you already hold is then returned as a bare ^pointer, never re-sent)","positions":"","pin":"451ed2608dfdc48704b00e02128d5037730c49f2","positions_consult":"{\"positions\":[]}","context_bytes":3377},"live_run_id":"2cc9ee85a67a","at":"2026-09-03T09:59:13Z"}
